Derived algorithms: VarInt size/writing, UTF-8 encoding, 21-bit frame length decoding and retained-buffer frame prepending.
ToolVisuals modifications: scoped opt-out and external-Krypton detection, native Minecraft adapters, strict fragmented frame validation, bounded framing, and JDK ByteBuffer-based outbound compression without packet-sized heap arrays.
The upstream Velocity Native compression/encryption backend, server entity tracker and leak-detector changes are not included. Existing vanilla decompression and cryptography remain in place; pipeline names/order and local connections are preserved.
Corresponding source: https://github.com/2twofactorauth3-star/ToolVisuals
Krypton credits prior work from Velocity and Paper. The frame bit-packing adaptation retains references to Netty PR 14050 and Hacker's Delight, section 2-1, as documented in the pinned upstream Varint21FrameDecoderMixin.java. Sources: https://github.com/netty/netty/pull/14050 and https://velocitypowered.com/ and https://papermc.io/.
